luation: Playing B1 is the safest option as it is a terminal tile not involved in any potential chows and minimizes risk of others completing their hands. Keeping W4, W5, W6 intact allows forming a chow for All Chows (2 points) while B7 pair offers potential for a pung.  \nReason: Discarding B1 avoids disrupting the W4-W5-W6 chow and maintains flexibility for forming additional melds. B1 has 3 remaining copies, reducing chance of others needing it.  \nAnswer: Play B1"}
