 play W6, as it's less likely to be taken for a Chi, and there are more left. That way, I can try to draw another W6 to form a pung. \n\nSo the answer would be to play W6.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing W6 is the optimal choice to reduce the risk of others forming a Chi while maintaining potential for future melds.  \nReason: Discarding W6 minimizes the chance of opponents completing a Chi (since W7 is already out), and with three W6s remaining, it allows flexibility to draw another for a pung later. Keeping W5 and W4 intact supports forming a chow (W4-W5-W6) if needed.  \nAnswer: Play W6"}
